      <h3 class="heading-md pt-4">What is an anagram?</h3>
      <p>
        If you have ever wondered <em>what is an anagram</em>, the <strong>anagram definition</strong> is straightforward: an anagram is a word or phrase created by rearranging the letters of another word or phrase, using every original letter once. “Listen” becomes “silent”, “evil” becomes “vile”, and “dormitory” becomes “dirty room”. The best anagram examples feel clever because the new phrase still makes sense, and sometimes even comments on the original. People have enjoyed this kind of wordplay for centuries, from ancient poets to modern crossword setters.
      </p>

      <h3 class="heading-md pt-4">Anagram generator, maker and creator in one</h3>
      <p>
        Many tools only handle single words. This <strong>anagram generator</strong> also builds multi-word results, so a short name can become several phrases. Think of it as an <strong>anagram maker</strong> and <strong>anagram creator</strong> for names, slogans, usernames, band names, pen names and puzzle clues. You stay in control with simple filters: set the minimum and maximum number of words, require a word with Must Include, ban words with Never Include, and choose whether to search only common vocabulary or the full dictionary. Common-words mode keeps results natural and puts the shortest anagrams first.
      </p>

